<article class="env-exercise" id="0EGA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EGA">Exercise <span data-tag="0EGA">111.46.2</span>.</a> Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field. Let $X$ be a smooth curve over $k$. Let $r \geq 1$. Show that the closed subset </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  D \subset X \times X^ r = X^{r + 1}  \]
</div>
  <p> whose closed points are the tuples $(x, x_1, \ldots , x_ r)$ with $x = x_ i$ for some $i$, has an invertible ideal sheaf. In other words, show that $D$ is an effective Cartier divisor. Hints: reduce to $r = 1$ and use that $X$ is a smooth curves to say something about the diagonal (look in books for this). </p>
</article>